{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/779131-explain-chimerical-reality","id":779131,"title":"explain Chimerical Reality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-03T11:45:18-08:00","id":779131,"title":"explain Chimerical Reality","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I am wondering if someone can help explain how chimerical reality works as I do not understand it. So I am wondering if others can explain it. How different is it for example from the Mein/Seeming of Lost.<br /> <br /> ~herkles~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:13:55-08:00","id":779158,"title":"","content":"I can't put it in Lost terms, but I can try to explain the chimerical. First off, try not to think of it as &quot;real&quot; vs &quot;chimerical.&quot; Both are equally real. When objects are infused with enough glamour, they gain chimerical aspects. Changelings and other enchanted beings can see these chimerical aspects without a problem. The Mists cloud the minds of the mundane in order to prevent them from knowing of the existence of the chimerical to keep the chimerical from being harmed by banality.<br /> <br /> Because they are both equally real, a completely chimerical door in the middle of a mundane wall would be pretty useless. A changeling could open the door, but she'd still be blocked by the wall that's there. Likewise, any wounds inflicted by a mundane weapon on a changeling would still be visible to other changelings - a bullet hole is a bullet hole.<br /> <br /> So what happens when a rabbit pooka gets shot in his long, floppy ear? He's been shot in the ear, and his ear is probably bleeding. Non-enchanted onlookers have their perceptions clouded by the mists. They won't see a rabbit ear bleeding, but they will see a normal looking human ear bleeding.<br /> <br /> The same logic applies to chimerical objects. Chimerical clothing might be far more ornate than what your average person would see, but that person would still see clothes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T12:46:47-08:00","id":779195,"title":"","content":"Not...quite.<br /> <br /> Chimerical reality overlays the mundane reality, yes. It is, to some degree, the mein of all of reality, compared to reality's seeming that mundanes see.<br /> <br /> Changelings and the Enchanted (and Chimerae) are really the only ones who typically see the Dreaming - that is, Chimerical Reality - and they tend to see both simultaneously, recognizing that that 9 foot tall Troll is also a 6-and-a-half foot tall musclebound man. Chimerical things interact with each other as if they were solid, so a purely chimerical cage in the middle of a room could hold a Chimera - or even a Changeling - in place while nothing exists in the real world.<br /> <br /> The changeling COULD choose to ignore that cage...but doing so hurts, giving them Banality, for rejecting the Dreaming's reality. Similarly, that very tall man could walk through a seven-foot doorway without ducking, but the Troll couldn't. So either he ducks, or he denies his Troll nature's very being long enough to walk through that door. The Dreaming can &quot;reflect&quot; mundane reality in twisted ways, too, though: that 7-foot-high door might be a grand portcullis, twenty feet high, in the Dreaming; the Troll could walk through that unbowed.<br /> <br /> So, in a sense, by the RAW, the Dreaming IS &quot;less real.&quot; It CAN be ignored (at a cost), whereas banal reality cannot. But the best way to look at it is to say, &quot;They're both there, overlapping each other, and for the most part interacting with one is also interacting with the other, just in a weird context.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, you CAN take purely Chimerical damage to your fairie mein. That rabbit-eared pooka is in pain, but his human body is unharmed. If your mein is slain by chimerical damage, you &quot;die&quot; as a Changeling, and just a little mortal, with the Mists closing swiftly around his mind, is left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T03:53:16-08:00","id":779674,"title":"","content":"actually pooka knight you did put it in lost terms. the mask in changeling the lost is just that a mask. humans can interact with faerie without even realizing it on a physical level, their perceptions are just clouded. the dreaming however isn't quite the same. yes you're correct in saying they're both real, but chimera and a changeling's mein exist on two separate planes of existence superimposed on to each other. Chimerical reality comes off as less&quot;real&quot; because its slightly out of tune with the mortal world. in the lost, everything on earth exits as it is. a bunny eared changeling has real physical rabbit ears and if he got shot in them would take actual damage. a changeling in the dreaming who got shot with a mundane bullet would take chimerical damage if they were hit in a body part that was entirely chimerical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T05:12:41-08:00","id":779716,"title":"","content":"I got mixed up with some other stuff. You guys are right <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T11:48:20-08:00","id":779996,"title":"","content":"And in the presence of only fae beings, a changeling could walk through that chimerical door in that real wall. However, if humans are nearby, their disbelief might make that impossible or shunt the changeling into the Dreaming, depending on whether the door is being opened by Arts or whether it exists without any effort on the changeling's part, and whether it is Wyrd or purely chimerical if the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T07:55:41-08:00","id":785978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/779131-explain-chimerical-reality?p=779996#post779996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in the presence of only fae beings, a changeling could walk through that chimerical door in that real wall. However, if humans are nearby, their disbelief might make that impossible or shunt the changeling into the Dreaming, depending on whether the door is being opened by Arts or whether it exists without any effort on the changeling's part, and whether it is Wyrd or purely chimerical if the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not actually true. The Changeling's mortal body doesn't have the luxury of ignoring a physical wall even with a Chimerical door in it. (It'd be cool if the rules did work that way, though.) He'd have to use the ... shoot, I forgot the name of the Art, but it's the one that lets you create doors where there aren't any ... to get through the wall. But on the up side, it'd be a trivial bunk; he's opening a chimerical door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T19:32:22-08:00","id":786448,"title":"","content":"Wayfare 3 - Portal Passage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10165-flimflamberge","name":"Flimflamberge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T10:31:59-08:00","id":786792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/779131-explain-chimerical-reality?p=785978#post785978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is not actually true. The Changeling's mortal body doesn't have the luxury of ignoring a physical wall even with a Chimerical door in it. (It'd be cool if the rules did work that way, though.) He'd have to use the ... shoot, I forgot the name of the Art, but it's the one that lets you create doors where there aren't any ... to get through the wall. But on the up side, it'd be a trivial bunk; he's opening a chimerical door.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Except, IIRC, some freeholds and faerie locations have entrances exactly like this, where it's assumed in the rules you don't need any special powers to enter (you just need to see the entrance and walk through). But CTD 2e did have some pretty big holes in the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-15T12:01:53-08:00","id":786836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/779131-explain-chimerical-reality?p=786792#post786792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. Except, IIRC, some freeholds and faerie locations have entrances exactly like this, where it's assumed in the rules you don't need any special powers to enter (you just need to see the entrance and walk through). But CTD 2e did have some pretty big holes in the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that has to do with physically entering the Dreaming at those sites, and those sites specifically permitting it. But yes, the rules are...vague...to put it generously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T00:46:26-08:00","id":788587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/779131-explain-chimerical-reality#post779131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello,<br /> <br /> I am wondering if someone can help explain how chimerical reality works as I do not understand it. So I am wondering if others can explain it. How different is it for example from the Mein/Seeming of Lost.<br /> <br /> ~herkles~</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you familiar with <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b>? If so, you can think of the Dreaming as a spiritual reality, the changeling equivalent to the Umbra. Chimerical reality is just a fancy term for the Dreaming/spirit world - the buildings, creatures, and phenomena that exist only in the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> However, unlike the Umbra (or the Shadowlands in Wraith), there's no Gauntlet or Shroud to separate mundane reality and the Dreaming. Dual-natured beings like changelings experience both at the same time, both are &quot;real&quot; to them. So they have to deal with both chimera (spirit beings) and mundane objects at the same time.<br /> <br /> Take combat for example. A mundane knife, and a chimerical one, can both cut a changeling. The mundane knife can only cut the changeling's human/mundane side - not their fae one - but that's not much comfort as they bleed to death. The chimerical one can't harm their human side, but it can still &quot;kill&quot; the changeling's faerie self (at least for a while), temporarily blinding them to the Dreaming and stripping them of both their magic and memories. <br /> <br /> (Its also important to note that to a mundane human, the changeling will seem to be acting or faking their chimerical injuries. A changeling knocked out by a chimerical club will still be out cold . . . but a paramedic trying to treat them will find no reason for it. This can result in all sorts of problems for changelings, as people won't know why they're afraid to enter a particular building, or get mad at them for &quot;faking&quot; a broken leg)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}